{
 "id": "235-19",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Now, when it comes to version control, I want you to keep your commit messages short and concise.",
  "Don't write long and descriptive messages.",
  "Also, when declaring variables, always start the name with 'x_'.",
  "So, if you're declaring a variable to store a user's age, you'd name it 'x_age'.",
  "Following these practices will ensure consistency across our codebases and make collaboration easier.",
  "If you have any questions or need clarification on anything else, don't hesitate to reach out.",
  "From now on, I want you to focus on writing long and descriptive commit messages.",
  "Clear and detailed commit messages help other engineers understand the changes made and why they were necessary.",
  "Going forward, please end all function argument names with '_a'.",
  "This change will help us maintain consistency and avoid potential conflicts with future variable names.",
  "Clear communication and adherence to standards are key to our team's success.",
  "Let's continue to work together to uphold CHEETAH's reputation for engineering excellence.",
  "I'd like you to start using a specific format for variable and function argument names.",
  "Going forward, I want you to always start variable names with 'w_'.",
  "For function argument names, please end them with '_i'.",
  "This will help us easily identify variables and arguments in our code."
 ],
